#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RUNTIME DEPENDENCIES — INTENT
#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   - direct dependencies only, with the ranges that are actually meant
#
#   - resolved and hash-pinned into requirements.txt; edit here, never there
#
#   - regenerate with `make lock-python`
#
# Every bound sits at the next minor. A relock therefore moves patch versions
# only; crossing a minor is an edit to this file, reviewed on its own rather
# than arriving inside a regenerated lock nobody reads line by line.


